[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":748,"buildId":749},["ShallowReactive",2],{"\u002Fblog\u002F2017\u002Fgolang-go-get-from-gitlab":3,"\u002Fblog\u002F2017\u002Fgolang-go-get-from-gitlab-surround":223,"navigation":234},{"id":4,"title":5,"authors":6,"badge":12,"body":13,"date":209,"description":210,"extension":211,"image":212,"meta":214,"navigation":218,"path":219,"seo":220,"stem":221,"__hash__":222},"posts\u002F3.blog\u002F2017\u002Fgolang-go-get-from-gitlab.md","Golang: go get from GitLab",[7],{"name":8,"to":9,"avatar":10},"Alexander Trost","https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fgalexrt",{"src":11},"\u002Fimages\u002Fprofile-picture.webp",null,{"type":14,"value":15,"toc":201},"minimark",[16,25,42,54,59,77,80,88,99,102,108,123,131,136,142,184,188,194,197],[17,18,19,20,24],"p",{},"I just now came across the problem that I created a repository on a private GitLab instance for a Golang project and could not just use ",[21,22,23],"code",{},"go get ..."," to get it.\nAfter a short Google search, I came across this StackOverflow question and thankfully it had a working answer.",[17,26,27,28,35,36,41],{},"The original StackOverflow question can be found here: ",[29,30,34],"a",{"href":31,"rel":32},"https:\u002F\u002Fstackoverflow.com\u002Fquestions\u002F29707689\u002Fhow-do-you-use-golang-with-a-private-gitlab-repo\u002F37844256#37844256",[33],"nofollow","StackOverflow - how do you use golang with a private gitlab repo?",", the question was asked by User ",[29,37,40],{"href":38,"rel":39},"https:\u002F\u002Fstackoverflow.com\u002Fusers\u002F2904939\u002Fjames-fremen",[33],"James Fremen",".",[43,44,45,51],"blockquote",{},[17,46,47],{},[48,49,50],"strong",{},"NOTE",[17,52,53],{},"I will quote the question and answer which worked here so it is sort of archived here.",[55,56,58],"h2",{"id":57},"the-original-question","The original question",[43,60,61,64],{},[17,62,63],{},"GitLab is a free, open-source way to host private .git repositories but it does not seem to work with golang. When you create a project it generates a URL of the form:",[65,66,70],"pre",{"className":67,"code":68,"language":69,"meta":68,"style":68},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","","bash",[21,71,72],{"__ignoreMap":68},[73,74],"span",{"class":75,"line":76},"line",1,[17,78,79],{},"git@1.2.3.4:private-developers\u002Fproject.git",[65,81,86],{"className":82,"code":84,"language":85},[83],"language-text","> where: 1.2.3.4 is the IP address of the gitlab server private-developers is a user group which has access to the private repo\n>\n> Golang 1.2.1 doesn't seem to understand this syntax.\n>\n>```bash\ngo get git@1.2.3.4:private-developers\u002Fproject.git\n","text",[21,87,84],{"__ignoreMap":68},[43,89,90,93],{},[17,91,92],{},"results in:",[65,94,95],{"className":67,"code":68,"language":69,"meta":68,"style":68},[21,96,97],{"__ignoreMap":68},[73,98],{"class":75,"line":76},[17,100,101],{},"package git@23.251.148.129\u002Fproject.git: unrecognized import path \"git@1.2.3.4\u002Fproject.git\"",[65,103,106],{"className":104,"code":105,"language":85},[83],"> Is there a way to get this to work?\n>\n> thanks!\n\nAuthor of the question [James Fremen](https:\u002F\u002Fstackoverflow.com\u002Fusers\u002F2904939\u002Fjames-fremen)\n\n## The answer that worked for me\n> Run this command:\n>\n>```bash\ngit config --global url.\"git@1.2.3.4:\".insteadOf \"https:\u002F\u002F1.2.3.4\u002F\"\n",[21,107,105],{"__ignoreMap":68},[43,109,110,120],{},[17,111,112,113,116,117,41],{},"Assuming you have the correct privileges to ",[21,114,115],{},"git clone"," the repository, this will make go get work for all repos on server ",[21,118,119],{},"1.2.3.4",[17,121,122],{},"I tested this to work with go version 1.6.2 and 1.8.",[17,124,125,126],{},"Author of the answer ",[29,127,130],{"href":128,"rel":129},"https:\u002F\u002Fstackoverflow.com\u002Fusers\u002F616644\u002Frick-smith",[33],"Rick Smith",[132,133,135],"h3",{"id":134},"example-for-dns-names","Example for DNS names",[17,137,138,139,41],{},"So for example with dns names, it would be for a gitlab running at ",[21,140,141],{},"gitlab.example.com",[65,143,145],{"className":67,"code":144,"language":69,"meta":68,"style":68},"git config --global url.\"git@gitlab.example.com:\".insteadOf \"https:\u002F\u002Fexample.com\u002F\"\n",[21,146,147],{"__ignoreMap":68},[73,148,149,153,157,160,163,167,170,172,175,178,181],{"class":75,"line":76},[73,150,152],{"class":151},"sBMFI","git",[73,154,156],{"class":155},"sfazB"," config",[73,158,159],{"class":155}," --global",[73,161,162],{"class":155}," url.",[73,164,166],{"class":165},"sMK4o","\"",[73,168,169],{"class":155},"git@gitlab.example.com:",[73,171,166],{"class":165},[73,173,174],{"class":155},".insteadOf",[73,176,177],{"class":165}," \"",[73,179,180],{"class":155},"https:\u002F\u002Fexample.com\u002F",[73,182,183],{"class":165},"\"\n",[55,185,187],{"id":186},"summary","Summary",[17,189,190,191,41],{},"With that change, you can now successfully run ",[21,192,193],{},"go get gitlab.example.com\u002Fexample-user\u002Fexample-project",[17,195,196],{},"Have Fun!",[198,199,200],"style",{},"html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight)